{
  "_about": "S9 THE TRADER WHO KNOWS (pool-laneS9), DARK. Read by Scripts/Surprise/TraderKnows.cs (StreamingAssets first, then Assets/Data). enabled=false = nothing runs. greeting: one line per camp visit per vendor in the shop panel's own message line, from the last death record (trader_deaths.json in the save dir; the game kept no death record before this). A line matches when every field it names matches (killer = creature id of whoever killed Joan, zone = zone id, weapon = item id the killer held, minCount = deaths to that killer in that zone); most matched fields wins, ties by weight with the seeded stream. {killer} {zone} {weapon} {mine} {count} {total} are filled from the names tables (unknown ids print greeting.unknown). sellBack: on the stalls in stallIds the Buy tab also lists the item Joan held in `slot` when she last died, only if she no longer owns it (sources in order; add killerWeapon to also offer what killed her); priceRows gives a market price to items with no market.json row (placeholder balance, Dom to set). impostor: seeded roll once per run (chancePerRun) picks one vendor by impostorWeight; at that stall the interact key spawns the creature (existing prefab) at the vendor and hides the vendor body; the corpse of the real vendor lies behind the stall (corpse.behindM) corpse.delayS after the impostor is dead; Joan leaving the camp restores the vendor. One surprise per zone visit through surprise_director.json (SurpriseGate). proof: harness args -s9:1 greeting with fakeDeath, -s9:2 impostor forced at impostorNpcId, -s9:3 both; the interact key is pressed for you after autoOpenAfterS in reach of the stall.",
